  "reconstructibility": 1,
  "reason": "The records strongly establish mechanical alloying followed by SPS, often at 1000 °C, as a suitable route for closely related Al–Co–Fe-containing high-entropy alloys, and they connect SPS with densification, diffusion, uniform microstructures, high hardness, and corrosion testing. Thus, applying 1000 °C SPS to ball-milled MgAlTiVFeCo would be plausible. However, none identifies the specific AlV2O4, FeAl2O4, and FeTiO3 barrier phases, their uniform precipitation at an optimum temperature, or the proposed continuous passive-film, chloride-blocking, parabolic oxidation mechanism. Reconstructing that specific structural mediator and mechanism would require a substantial new idea."
